Package: amber-gtk4
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Andre Bremer <hyperquader@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @DEPS@
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Hyperquader-Coders/amber-gtk4
Description: GTK4 runtime bundle for the amber suite
 One GTK4 build shared by the amber applications, installed to
 /usr/lib/amber-gtk4 and reached only through those applications'
 RUNPATH. It is deliberately not on the ldconfig path, so installing it
 cannot change what anything else on the system links against.
 .
 It exists because kat800's terminal widget (VTE) needs a newer GTK than
 Linux Mint ships, and maintaining one build for the suite beats
 maintaining one per application. The version is held at 4.16 on purpose:
 4.18 requires a newer pango and glib than Mint has, and bundling those
 too is a cascade this package exists to avoid.
 .
 This is a runtime bundle, not a development package. Build against the
 distro's libgtk-4-dev.
